## Quality Gate fix — Deno lockfile v5 + Node 24 action upgrades

### Root cause

The `deno.lock` committed in this PR uses **lockfile format version 5**, which is only understood by Deno 2.x. The CI workflow was installing `deno-version: v1.x`, causing an immediate failure:

```
error: Unsupported lockfile version '5'. Try upgrading Deno or recreating the lockfile …
```

### Changes applied

**`.github/workflows/ci.yml`** — three targeted updates:

| Item | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| `deno-version` | `v1.x` | `v2.x` |
| `actions/checkout` | `34e1148…` (v4.3.1, Node 20) | `de0fac2…` (v6.0.2, Node 24) |
| `actions/setup-node` | `49933ea…` (v4.x, Node 20) | `48b55a0…` (v6.4.0, Node 24) |

The `actions/checkout` and `actions/setup-node` upgrades also address the Node 20 deprecation warnings — GitHub is forcing Node 24 from **2026-06-02** (six days away).

### Verification

`./quality.sh` ran cleanly locally:
- **141/141** Node.js tests pass (including all CI workflow checks)
- **44/44** Deno tests pass under `deno test --frozen`
